Subject: Port: friends between the releases, by a friend code of any release
Upstream-base: a353c8f2dfb34eb08fecd725965a46ea629428e3

A friend code is a GameSpy profile id under 7 bits of a hash over that id
and the game code of the release that made it (DWC_CreateFriendKey): a
CRC-8 in the USA's, Europe's and Japan's DWC, an MD5 in Korea's, whose
DWC_Acc_CreateFriendKey and DWC_Acc_CheckFriendKey take the generator as a
third argument. DWC checks a code with its own game's game code only: the
friend roster refuses another release's code as invalid
(FriendManager::AddFriendKey), and DWC_GetGsProfileId would find no
profile in it anyway, so DWC would never ask the server for that friend
(addbuddy), nor match their status or accept their request.

Online, the port's games of every release meet (tweak patch 0058), and the
WFC server pairs friends by profile id alone. DWC_CheckFriendKey,
DWC_Acc_FriendKeyToGsProfileId and DWC_GetGsProfileId, which every check
of a code goes through, now first take a code that any release makes for
its profile, before their own checks, which differ between the releases.
Making codes stays as it was, so every player keeps the code they see, and
a friend of another release goes through the original states: a friend
code until both have added each other, which DWC then turns into the
friend's profile id. A mistyped code is now taken by chance about five
times out of 128 instead of once.

The roster's check for the player's own code compares whole codes; their
own profile under another release's code is now taken as their own too.

